# W4 wiring for agentrix-node: Assess, the claim and the Move render agentrix-onboarding's pages.
#
# Apply on platform after the first release's handover (assess/ is the first release Assess and broker's, claim/ the
# control-plane session's, pages/ the first release spec's): `git apply specs/platform/patches/w4-assess-wiring.patch`.
# Made against platform 6c621a7 (node already depends on agentrix-onboarding and mounts it in
# wiring/host.rs). With it applied on W4's branch node's lib tests pass (134); Assess and the
# signed-in claim page were checked through a local node, the Move page in W4's preview.
#
# - assess/mod.rs: AssessState::with_pages(Arc<Pages>); GET /assess beside POST; Start and
#   Assess render through Pages when set, the console's templates otherwise.
# - claim/mod.rs: ClaimState.pages (Option); the claim page renders through Pages when set.
# - pages/mod.rs: PagesState.onboarding (Option); /console/move renders through Pages when set
#   (tests and the doc example pass None).
# - app.rs: one Pages for all three. Styles and scripts come through agentrix_onboarding::mount.
#
